      "content": "but that's the thing, i don't want \"the next hour\" or \"the next year.\" what's the point of just existing when the thing that made my existence meaningful is just gone? everyone's going to look at me and see a failure. it feels so much easier to just... stop everything before the shame fully sets in. like, why drag out the humiliation of trying to rebuild something that's already broken? wouldn't it just be more dignified to just end the story here?",
